<title>TURKEY: Turkish central bank reserve up $274 mln wk/wk.</title>
<headline>Turkish central bank reserve up $274 mln wk/wk.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish central bank said on Thursday its foreign currency reserves rose by $274 million to $17.547 billion in the week to November 29.</p>
<p>Figures in billion dollar</p>
<p>		   November 29    November 22  end-1995</p>
<p> Forex reserve   17.547	  17.273	 12.391</p>
<p> Gold reserve     1.383	   1.383	  1.383</p>
<p> Total reserve   18.930	  18.656	 13.774</p>
<p>Gross international reserves, including gold and commercial bank holdings, rose by $17 million to $27.694 billion in the week ending November 15, the bank said.</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
